# Khadas Edge1 - shared memory through memfd, not ashmem.
#
# Installed on /product, not /vendor, on purpose: init runs the commands of product
# rc files itself, while vendor ones go through vendor_init, which may not set this
# system property. And init reads /product/etc/init after /system/etc/init/hw/init.rc,
# so this post-fs-data action runs after init.rc's own - which is the point:
#
#   on post-fs-data
#       # sys.memfd_use set to false by default, ...
#       setprop sys.use_memfd false
#
# That line overrode the build.prop value the tenth card shipped, and getprop on the
# board read sys.use_memfd=false while every ashmem region kept failing (device.mk,
# "Shared memory", has the rest). Everything that uses shared memory in earnest -
# zygote, system_server, SurfaceFlinger and the composer - starts after this.
on post-fs-data
    setprop sys.use_memfd true
